    "bio": "a Representative from Minnesota; born in Fargo, Cass County, N.Dak., February 8, 1930; graduated from Moorhead High School, Moorhead, Minn., 1948; farmer; member, Barnesville, Minn., school board, 1976-1977; member, Minnesota state house of representatives, 1966-1975; delegate, Minnesota state Republican conventions, 1964-1968; elected as a Republican to the Ninety-fifth Congress, by special election, to fill the vacancy caused by the resignation of United States Representative Robert Selmer Bergland, and reelected to the six succeeding Congresses (February 22, 1977-January 3, 1991); unsuccessful candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Second Congress in 1990; was a resident of Barnesville, Minn.; died on July 2, 2013, in Detroit Lakes, Minn.; interment at Comstock Lutheran Cemetery, near Comstock, Minn.",
